From: Marco Müller <hello@annoyedmilk.ch>
Subject: [PATCH] iomap: keep four entries in the ioend mempools

Each of the two ioend bio sets preallocated 32 bios with a bio_vec of
256 entries: 192 KiB on a machine with 16 MiB, whose ext4 root does not
write through iomap at all.  The pools are the reserve for forward
progress under memory pressure, and four entries in each are enough for
that.
---
diff --git a/fs/iomap/ioend.c b/fs/iomap/ioend.c
--- a/fs/iomap/ioend.c
+++ b/fs/iomap/ioend.c
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@
 
 static int __init iomap_ioend_init(void)
 {
-	const unsigned int nr_mempool_entries = 4 * (PAGE_SIZE / SECTOR_SIZE);
+	const unsigned int nr_mempool_entries = 4;
 	int error;
 
 	error = bioset_init(&iomap_ioend_bioset, nr_mempool_entries,
